       Parameters currently recognised by built‐in KDFs are as follows. Not
       all parameters are relevant to, or are understood by all KDFs:

       "size" (OOSSSSLL__KKDDFF__PPAARRAAMM__SSIIZZEE) <unsigned integer>
           Gets the output size from the associated KDF ctx.  If the algorithm
           produces  a variable amount of output, SIZE_MAX should be returned.
           If the input parameters required to calculate the fixed output size
           have not yet been supplied, 0  should  be  returned  indicating  an
           error.

       "key" (OOSSSSLL__KKDDFF__PPAARRAAMM__KKEEYY) <octet string>
           Sets the key in the associated KDF ctx.

       "secret" (OOSSSSLL__KKDDFF__PPAARRAAMM__SSEECCRREETT) <octet string>
           Sets the secret in the associated KDF ctx.

       "pass" (OOSSSSLL__KKDDFF__PPAARRAAMM__PPAASSSSWWOORRDD) <octet string>
           Sets the password in the associated KDF ctx.

       "cipher" (OOSSSSLL__KKDDFF__PPAARRAAMM__CCIIPPHHEERR) <UTF8 string>
       "digest" (OOSSSSLL__KKDDFF__PPAARRAAMM__DDIIGGEESSTT) <UTF8 string>
       "mac" (OOSSSSLL__KKDDFF__PPAARRAAMM__MMAACC) <UTF8 string>
           Sets  the  name of the underlying cipher, digest or MAC to be used.
           It must name a suitable algorithm for the KDF that’s being used.

       "maclen" (OOSSSSLL__KKDDFF__PPAARRAAMM__MMAACC__SSIIZZEE) <octet string>
           Sets the length of the MAC in the associated KDF ctx.

       "properties" (OOSSSSLL__KKDDFF__PPAARRAAMM__PPRROOPPEERRTTIIEESS) <UTF8 string>
           Sets the  properties  to  be  queried  when  trying  to  fetch  the
           underlying  algorithm.   This  must  be  given  together  with  the
           algorithm naming parameter to be considered valid.

       "iter" (OOSSSSLL__KKDDFF__PPAARRAAMM__IITTEERR) <unsigned integer>
           Sets the number of iterations in the associated KDF ctx.

       "mode" (OOSSSSLL__KKDDFF__PPAARRAAMM__MMOODDEE) <UTF8 string>
           Sets the mode in the associated KDF ctx.

       "pkcs5" (OOSSSSLL__KKDDFF__PPAARRAAMM__PPKKCCSS55) <integer>
           Enables or disables the SP800-132 compliance checks.  A mode  of  0
           enables the compliance checks.

           The checks performed are:

           - the iteration count is at least 1000.
           - the salt length is at least 128 bits.
           - the derived key length is at least 112 bits.
       "ukm" (OOSSSSLL__KKDDFF__PPAARRAAMM__UUKKMM) <octet string>
           Sets  an  optional  random  string  that  is provided by the sender
           called "partyAInfo".  In CMS this is the user keying material.

